## The Bible plugin as the app lists it, its cover and its settings (src/plugin.rs, src/plugin_config.rs).

plugin-name = Bible
plugin-description = Read the Bible, highlight and annotate verses, and quote them with /ref.
plugin-cover-title = Bible
config-default-bible = Default Bible
config-default-bible-help = Translation opened when you create a new tab.
config-cross-refs = Advanced cross-references
config-cross-refs-help = Shows the icon and the list with every fetch.bible reference. TSK notes (letters a/b/c) always show.
config-cross-refs-level = Depth of the cross-references
config-cross-refs-level-help = fetch.bible ranks its references by relevance and offers three sets: Essential keeps the most relevant third, Balanced two thirds, Complete every one. Changing it downloads the references of your Bibles again.
config-cross-refs-level-small = Essential
config-cross-refs-level-medium = Balanced
config-cross-refs-level-large = Complete
config-originals = Original languages
config-originals-help = Shows the Hebrew or Greek behind each verse: every word with its pronunciation, what it means here and in general, and where else it appears. Turning it on downloads about 13 MB (STEPBible, CC BY 4.0) that stay on this device.
